.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ── OS cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Secrets / local env ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*

# ── Agent instruction files (Claude Code and others) ─────────────────────────
# Kept local rather than public: CLAUDE.md documents detection internals/
# limitations (e.g. exactly what the PDF flow does and doesn't auto-detect) -
# not a secret, but not something we want to hand a public roadmap of to
# anyone who clones/forks this repo either. Untracked as of 2026-08-25; still
# read locally by Claude Code, just no longer synced to GitHub going forward.
# AGENTS.md followed on 2026-10-30 for the same reason; the rules that matter
# to every contributor are in CONTRIBUTING.md and enforced by tests.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# ── Legacy source (excluded from packaging too) ──────────────────────────────
_legacy/

# ── Sensitive data — NEVER commit ────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is a PII tool. Real input documents, everything it writes out, and the
# master list (real staff names + IDs) are Confidential under IPA's
# data-classification policy and must never enter version control. The app
# reads the master list from a local file each machine supplies out-of-band;
# MasterListRepository tolerates its absence. Tests build their own made-up
# files at run time, so none of these formats needs to be tracked.
#
# Documents (inputs and redacted outputs alike):
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm
*.xlsb
*.ods
*.pdf
*.docx
*.doc
*.odt
*.rtf
# Every CSV/TSV: the name crosswalk (`*_crosswalk.csv`, Excel/Word, and the
# opt-in PDF names file) is the re-identification key, and the PDF label
# mapping (`*_mapping.csv`) decodes the labels together with the master list.
# The repo has no CSV of its own.
*.csv
*.tsv
# Screenshots and scans can show real documents. Images the repo does need
# live under assets/ or docs/images/ and must be made up.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
!assets/**
!docs/images/**
# data/ is the local-only drop point for the master list and real input
# documents: ignore everything in it whatever the extension, keep the README.
data/*
!data/README.md

# ── Frontend (React UI) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The built bundle in finance_redactor/presentation/static/ IS committed, so
# end users need no Node; CI checks it matches frontend/.
node_modules/
frontend/coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
npm-debug.log*
*.log
